    "honest_label": "nine (zone, year) cells. FINDING C13-D rests on 44. A cross-cell rank correlation on nine points has a sampling sd of roughly 0.38 under independence, so a cross-cell claim from this window is **not established**; the per-day columns are this cycle's evidence. Read the sign carefully: the cross-cell correlation of a RES predictor against error_over_headroom is NEGATIVE while every per-day within-cell one is POSITIVE, and that is not a scale artefact \u2014 it survives normalising by each cell's own mean residual load (*_over_mean). The two measure different things. BETWEEN cells, a zone-year with a larger relative RES swing has a wider price spread and so more headroom, which makes it easier. WITHIN a cell, a day whose RES publication was revised more than usual is harder. Use the *_over_mean columns for any cross-zone sentence anyway: the raw-MW ones are also size proxies (NO2's mean residual load is 3.6 GW against DE-LU's 30.0).",
